{"content":"## Fixed: the clipboard subprocess is time-bounded (writer + reader)

`lib/src/cli/clipboard_writer.dart`:

- every path in the `writeClipboardText` loop is wrapped in `.timeout(processTimeout)` (new parameter, default `pasteboardProcessTimeout` = 5 s) — a wedged writer (shadowed `pbcopy`, `xclip` on a dead `$DISPLAY`) can no longer hold the future, so `_handleProviderExportCommand`'s `_providerFlowActive` gate always releases;
- a `TimeoutException` falls through to the next path (the loop's fallthrough home) and is remembered: the final failure is the named `PasteboardWriteUnavailable('clipboard writer timed out')` instead of blaming the tooling;
- the default `_runWithStdin` runner additionally **kills** the wedged process on expiry (`boundedPasteboardWait` in the shared `pasteboard_platform.dart`) — no one-process-per-call leak.

Same fix in the gh-1575 reader: `clipboard_reader.dart`'s `_runBinaryProcess` is bounded by the same shared helper; its `TimeoutException` lands in the existing dispatch catch as the named unavailable.

Tests (`test/cli/clipboard_writer_test.dart`): `a wedged writer times out into the named unavailable` (hanging injected runner + 50 ms bound → reason `clipboard writer timed out`) and `a timed-out path falls through to the next one` (xclip wedges, wl-copy still lands the write). Clipboard+paste suites 61/61; `dart analyze` clean; scoped CRAP for `writeClipboardText` 6.00 @ 100% cov.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_5_clipboard_timeout.md"}

